Golem: a swipe to another workspace does not give the keyboard to the window
under the pointer when that workspace already has its window focused.

At the end of a workspace swipe Hyprland calls InputManager::refocus(), a
pointer move that FOCUSES the window under the cursor whatever follow_mouse
says. CMonitor::changeWorkspace has just focused the workspace's last used
window; with follow_mouse = 2 (Golem's: the keyboard is detached from the
pointer) the refocus then moved the keyboard to the window under the cursor,
often one BEHIND the focused one. waverunner's focus memory (focus_cycle.rs,
settle_target) gave it back ~100 ms later — and in between the covered window
was active: its dim lifted, its border lit, and it blinked.

Measured on the dev box 2026-10-21 (waveview's FOCUS trace + the compositor's
events): workspace change → foot (reason WORKSPACE_CHANGE), +0.5 ms → seam
under the pointer (reason CLICK = refocus), +97 ms → foot again (a dispatch).
Only when the pointer rested over the covered window — "not always".

Now: with follow_mouse != 1 and a window already focused on the workspace
arrived at, only the pointer's focus is updated (simulateMouseMovement). An
empty workspace, or follow_mouse = 1, behave as before.

Golem's own; keep.

diff -ru a/src/managers/input/UnifiedWorkspaceSwipeGesture.cpp b/src/managers/input/UnifiedWorkspaceSwipeGesture.cpp
--- a/src/managers/input/UnifiedWorkspaceSwipeGesture.cpp	2026-10-21 03:04:08.921840832 +0000
+++ b/src/managers/input/UnifiedWorkspaceSwipeGesture.cpp	2026-10-21 03:04:08.944855462 +0000
@@ -302,7 +302,22 @@
     m_workspaceBegin   = nullptr;
     m_initialDirection = 0;
 
-    g_pInputManager->refocus();
+    // Golem: the workspace change above has ALREADY focused that workspace's own
+    // window (the one last used there). A full refocus then handed the KEYBOARD to
+    // whatever window was under the pointer — with follow_mouse = 2, where the
+    // pointer does not carry the keyboard, often a window BEHIND the one just
+    // focused: it lit up, then waverunner gave the focus back ~100 ms later, and
+    // the covered window "blinked" (Max, 2026-10-21: "when I slide to a workspace
+    // with a window on top of another the covered one blinks… not always" — only
+    // when the pointer rested over the covered one). With the keyboard detached
+    // from the pointer and a window already focused on the workspace arrived at,
+    // only the POINTER's focus is brought up to date.
+    static auto PFOLLOWMOUSE = CConfigValue<Config::INTEGER>("input:follow_mouse");
+    const auto  FOCUSED      = Desktop::focusState()->window();
+    if (*PFOLLOWMOUSE != 1 && FOCUSED && FOCUSED->m_workspace == pSwitchedTo)
+        g_pInputManager->simulateMouseMovement();
+    else
+        g_pInputManager->refocus();
 
     // apply alpha
     for (auto const& ls : Desktop::focusState()->monitor()->m_layerSurfaceLayers[2]) {
